# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# NOTE: the previous `/* /index.html 200` rule made every unknown URL return the
# homepage with HTTP 200 (a "soft 404"), which wastes crawl budget and can cause
# duplicate-content dilution. Next.js `output: 'export'` already emits a real
# HTML file per route and Cloudflare Pages serves the generated 404.html for
# unknown paths, so no SPA fallback is required.
#
# Trailing-slash normalisation: redirect explicit index.html requests to the
# canonical directory URL so only one URL form is indexed.
/publications/index.html /publications/ 301
/awards/index.html /awards/ 301
/cv/index.html /cv/ 301
